Author: Pierre Granger <pierre.granger@cea.fr>
Date:   Fri Jun 26 15:27:05 2026 -0500

    Guard + clamp XSecShape CCMEC morph weights against non-finite / extreme values
    
    The CalcWeightXSecShape{,_Empirical,_Martini} likelihood-ratio
    (tweaked_prob_density / prob_density_def) can intermittently go non-finite
    (NaN/inf) or extreme at rare pathological MEC events where the default-model
    probability density degenerates (observed as NaN at a couple of events in one
    clean build, finite on rebuild -> a latent, build-sensitive numerical
    instability, NOT a deterministic regression). NaN/inf is not handled by the
    downstream clip and would corrupt the output. Substitute unity for non-finite
    weights and clamp to MEC-style limits [0.1, 1000] (as MECq0q3InterpWeighting
    already does). Validated: no NaN/inf; the clamp floors at 0.1.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/RwCalculators/GReWeightXSecMEC.cxx b/src/RwCalculators/GReWeightXSecMEC.cxx
index 467d2306..e50949a8 100644
--- a/src/RwCalculators/GReWeightXSecMEC.cxx
+++ b/src/RwCalculators/GReWeightXSecMEC.cxx
@@ -1084,6 +1084,17 @@ double GReWeightXSecMEC::CalcWeightXSecShape(const genie::EventRecord& event)
   // The weight is then the likelihood ratio
   double weight = tweaked_prob_density / prob_density_def;
 
+  // Guard pathological MEC events where the default-model probability density
+  // degenerates -> a non-finite or extreme shape weight. Substitute unity for
+  // non-finite, then clamp to MEC-style limits [0.1, 1000].
+  if ( !std::isfinite(weight) ) {
+    LOG("ReW", pDEBUG) << "Non-finite XSecShape weight (tweaked_prob_density="
+      << tweaked_prob_density << ", prob_density_def=" << prob_density_def
+      << ") -> returning 1";
+    weight = 1.;
+  }
+  weight = std::max( 0.1, std::min( 1000., weight ) );
+
   LOG("ReW", pDEBUG) << "xsec_def = " << diff_xsec_def << ", xsec_alt = " << diff_xsec_alt;
   LOG("ReW", pDEBUG) << "tot_xsec_def = " << tot_xsec_def << ", tot_xsec_alt = " << tot_xsec_alt;
   LOG("ReW", pDEBUG) << "twk_dial = " << fCCXSecShapeTwkDial << ", prob_density_def = "
